                                                                               
 Usage: forge [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...                                      
                                                                               
 ForgeFlow 2.0 - durable, verifiable and evaluable AI coding harness.          
                                                                               
┌─ Options ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ --version  -V        Show version and exit.                                 │
│ --help               Show this message and exit.                            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
┌─ Commands ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ init       Initialize ForgeFlow state without overwriting project files.    │
│ goal       Compile and persist a goal, revision and dependency DAG.         │
│ plan       Show the hard-dependency DAG, waves and ready frontier.          │
│ run        Execute the ready frontier with independent verification.        │
│ quick      Compile a risk-scoped quick plan and run it (gates are never     │
│            skipped).                                                        │
│ status     Show durable task, gate and recovery status.                     │
│ verify     Run trusted verifier commands and evaluate all contract gates.   │
│ resume     Recover expired leases and requeue safely resumable work.        │
│ recover    Inspect interrupted/blocked tasks and required manual actions.   │
│ context    Build an explainable, budgeted context bundle.                   │
│ explain    Trace which test and source version support one acceptance       │
│            criterion.                                                       │
│ pause      Pause a running goal without losing task leases or events.       │
│ cancel     Cancel a goal and all unfinished tasks.                          │
│ benchmark  Run the reproducible internal fixture benchmark and ablations.   │
│ deliver    Build a READY/BLOCKED delivery manifest and evidence index.      │
│ doctor     Check toolchain, persistence, git and external integration       │
│            readiness.                                                       │
│ events     Inspect append-only domain events.                               │
│ policy     Offline policy validation, activation and rollback.              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

